<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuiabá</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cuiabá is the capital of the Brazilian state of Mato Grosso, near the geographical centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. It was founded in 1719 after bandeirantes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> found gold in the area, and miners reached it by long river convoys. It replaced Vila Bela as the capital of Mato Grosso in 1835.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuiaba.jpg" alt="Cuiabá" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arne Müseler · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cuiab%C3%A1_center.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
